{
  "note": "Byte-identical vendor of 4 npm packages (@sigstore/core, @sigstore/bundle, @sigstore/protobuf-specs, @sigstore/verify), laid out as a hand-placed node_modules/@sigstore/* tree so each package's own bare `require(\"@sigstore/...\")` calls resolve via Node's standard node_modules walk-up — zero `npm install`, zero rewritten import paths (STANDING ORDERS #10). Each package ships already-compiled CommonJS dist/ output from its npm tarball (no build step run here). Every tarball was downloaded directly from registry.npmjs.org and its sha1 checked against the registry's own published `dist.shasum` before being unpacked (see npmTarballShasum per entry). Also covers the pinned Sigstore trust-root data file (see the pinned-trust-data entry) — HELM-SIGSTORE-OFFLINE-VERIFY-1.",
